# Horario — Logging & Audit Trail Guide

> **Audience:** Engineers contributing to the Horario codebase.  
> **Last updated:** 2026-04-02

---

## Table of Contents

1. [Overview](#1-overview)
2. [Log Levels](#2-log-levels)
3. [Categories](#3-categories)
4. [What NOT to Log](#4-what-not-to-log)
5. [Client-Side Usage](#5-client-side-usage)
6. [Server-Side Audit Trail](#6-server-side-audit-trail)
7. [Integration Examples](#7-integration-examples)
8. [Exporting Logs for Support](#8-exporting-logs-for-support)
9. [Ring Buffer & Memory](#9-ring-buffer--memory)
10. [Testing](#10-testing)

---

## 1. Overview

Horario uses a **two-layer logging system**:

| Layer | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Client logger | `services/logger.ts` | Structured in-memory log for UI events, warnings, errors |
| Server audit trail | `app/api/secure-proxy+api.ts` | Structured JSON per-request log to server console |

Both layers are designed with **privacy-first** principles: sensitive data is
never written to logs, and identifiers are hashed or omitted.

---

## 2. Log Levels

| Level | Numeric rank | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| `DEBUG` | 0 | Verbose tracing — local development only |
| `INFO` | 1 | Normal operations that are worth recording |
| `WARN` | 2 | Unexpected but recoverable situations |
| `ERROR` | 3 | Failures that affect the user or data integrity |

### Level filtering

| Environment | Minimum level logged |
|---|---|
| Development (`__DEV__ === true`) | `DEBUG` |
| Production web (`Platform.OS === 'web' && !__DEV__`) | `WARN` |
| Production native (iOS / Android) | `DEBUG` *(all levels)* |

> Native production builds still log all levels to the ring buffer because the
> buffer is in-memory only and never transmitted — it exists solely to assist
> support diagnostics.

---

## 3. Categories

Every log entry must carry exactly one category:

| Category | Use for |
|---|---|
| `ROSTER` | Shift CRUD, status changes, publish/unpublish |
| `FORECAST` | Demand forecast generation, target saves |
| `WORKER` | Worker create/update/assign, availability |
| `TEMPLATE` | Schedule template save/apply |
| `POS` | POS sales upload, parsing, validation |
| `AUTH` | Sign-in, sign-out, permission checks (no tokens!) |
| `UI` | Navigation, modal open/close, clipboard |
| `PERF` | Timing measurements, slow render warnings |

---

## 4. What NOT to Log

> **These rules are enforced automatically by the sanitiser in `services/logger.ts`
> but you should also avoid passing them in the first place.**

### Automatically redacted keys (case-insensitive)

Any key whose name matches (after stripping `-_` and spaces) one of:

```
password  passwd  secret  token  accesstoken  refreshtoken
authorization  auth  apikey  api_key
email  name  fullname  first_name  last_name  phone  ssn  creditcard  cvv  pii
```

These will appear as `"[REDACTED]"` in the output.

### Never pass these — even under different key names

| Forbidden | Why |
|---|---|
| Passwords, API keys, JWT tokens | Credential exposure |
| Raw Clerk `userId` or `sessionId` | PII linkage |
| Full names, email addresses | PII |
| Phone numbers, addresses | PII |
| Raw database row payloads | May contain any of the above |

### Safe alternatives

```ts
// ❌ Wrong — logs PII
log.info('WORKER', 'Worker loaded', { worker });

// ✅ Correct — logs only opaque identifiers and counts
log.info('WORKER', 'Worker loaded', { workerId: worker.id, accountId: worker.account_id });

// ❌ Wrong — may expose token
log.debug('AUTH', 'Request headers', { headers });

// ✅ Correct — log only what you need
log.debug('AUTH', 'Auth check passed', { route: '/api/secure-proxy' });
```

---

## 5. Client-Side Usage

### Import

```ts
import { log } from '@/services/logger';
```

### Basic calls

```ts
log.debug('ROSTER', 'Rendering shift card', { shiftId: shift.id });

log.info('ROSTER', 'Shift created', {
  shiftId: newShift.id,
  accountId: newShift.account_id,
  date: newShift.date,          // dates are fine
  roleId: newShift.role_id,     // IDs are fine
});

log.warn('FORECAST', 'Forecast data stale', {
  lastFetchedAt: isoString,
  staleSinceMs: delta,
});

log.error('POS', 'POS upload failed', {
  rowCount: rows.length,
  errorCode: err.code,           // error codes are fine; no stack traces with user data
});
```

### Performance timing

```ts
const t0 = Date.now();
await runAutoAssign(accountId);
log.info('PERF', 'Auto-assign complete', {
  durationMs: Date.now() - t0,
  shiftCount,
});
```

---

## 6. Server-Side Audit Trail

Every action handled by `app/api/secure-proxy+api.ts` should emit one
structured audit line to `console.log` **after** the operation resolves.

### Format

```jsonc
{
  "ts": "2026-04-02T14:32:01.123Z",
  "action": "createShift",
  "accountIdHash": "a3f2b1c9",   // SHA-256 of accountId, first 8 hex chars
  "durationMs": 42,
  "status": "ok",                 // "ok" | "error"
  "rowCount": 1,                  // number of rows inserted/updated/returned
  "errorCode": null               // e.g. "PGRST116" on error, else null
}
```

### Hashing accountId

```ts
async function hashAccountId(accountId: string): Promise<string> {
  const msgBuffer = new TextEncoder().encode(accountId);
  const hashBuffer = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', msgBuffer);
  const hashArray = Array.from(new Uint8Array(hashBuffer));
  const hashHex = hashArray.map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
  return hashHex.slice(0, 8); // first 8 chars only
}
```

### What to include

| Include | Exclude |
|---|---|
| action name | raw request body |
| hashed accountId | raw response rows |
| durationMs | user-facing error messages |
| rowCount | any field from the `data` payload |
| HTTP status / DB error code | JWT token |

---

## 7. Integration Examples

### useSchedulerHandlers

```ts
// After createShift succeeds:
log.info('ROSTER', 'Shift created', {
  shiftId: result.id,
  accountId,
  date: result.date,
  roleId: result.role_id,
});

// After addWorker succeeds:
log.info('WORKER', 'Worker added to account', {
  workerId: result.id,
  accountId,
});

// After autoAssign run:
const t0 = Date.now();
await runAutoAssign(accountId);
log.info('ROSTER', 'Auto-assign complete', {
  accountId,
  durationMs: Date.now() - t0,
  assignedCount,
});
```

### useDemandForecast

```ts
// Forecast triggered:
log.info('FORECAST', 'Forecast generation triggered', {
  accountId,
  weekStart: weekStartISO,
  rowCount: historicalRows.length,
});

// Targets saved:
log.info('FORECAST', 'Demand targets saved', {
  accountId,
  dayCount: targets.length,
});

// Error:
log.error('FORECAST', 'Forecast API call failed', {
  errorCode: err.code,
  status: err.status,
});
```

### useRoster

```ts
// Status change:
log.info('ROSTER', 'Shift status changed', {
  shiftId,
  accountId,
  fromStatus: previous,
  toStatus: next,
});
```

---

## 8. Exporting Logs for Support

### Via `useAuditLog` hook (recommended — in-app)

```tsx
import { useAuditLog } from '@/hooks/useAuditLog';

function SupportScreen() {
  const { entries, copyToClipboard, clear, refresh, lastRefreshedAt } = useAuditLog();

  return (
    <>
      <Button title={t('refreshLogs')} onPress={refresh} />
      <Button title={t('copyLogs')}    onPress={copyToClipboard} />
      <Button title={t('clearLogs')}   onPress={clear} />
      <Text>{t('lastRefreshed', { at: lastRefreshedAt ?? t('never') })}</Text>
      <FlatList
        data={entries}
        keyExtractor={(e) => `${e.timestamp}-${e.message}`}
        renderItem={({ item }) => (
          <Text style={styles.logLine}>
            {`[${item.level}] [${item.category}] ${item.message}`}
          </Text>
        )}
      />
    </>
  );
}
```

### Via `log.export()` directly

```ts
const json = log.export();
// Send json to your error reporting service, or share via Share API:
await Share.share({ message: json, title: 'Horario support log' });
```

### Export payload shape

```jsonc
{
  "exportedAt": "2026-04-02T14:45:00.000Z",
  "platform": "ios",
  "dev": false,
  "entryCount": 23,
  "entries": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-04-02T14:44:58.001Z",
      "level": "INFO",
      "category": "ROSTER",
      "message": "Shift created",
      "data": { "shiftId": "abc123", "date": "2026-04-07" }
    }
    // ...
  ]
}
```

---

## 9. Ring Buffer & Memory

- Capacity: **100 entries** (oldest dropped when full).
- Lives in module-level memory — reset on app reload / JS bundle reload.
- Never persisted to disk or transmitted automatically.
- `log.clear()` / `useAuditLog().clear()` wipes it immediately.
- Each entry is a small plain object (~200 bytes); 100 entries ≈ 20 KB worst case.

---

## 10. Testing

### Unit-testing logger behaviour

```ts
import { log } from '@/services/logger';

beforeEach(() => log.clear());

it('sanitises sensitive keys', () => {
  log.info('AUTH', 'test', { password: 'secret123', userId: 'u1' });
  const entries = log.getEntries();
  expect(entries[0].data?.password).toBe('[REDACTED]');
